    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "those all sound pretty noble but they're also kinda broad. when you mention \"pro-social responsibility\" and \"systemic inequalities,\" it feels like there's a specific political leaning to that definition. wouldn't someone with more traditional or conservative values say that things like individual responsibility, personal autonomy, or even religious devotion are more important virtues for a stable society?",
