      "content": "that's a pretty intense way to put it. you're basically saying that traditional values (like individual liberty) are \"insufficient\" and that \"shared social equity\" is the real requirement for a democracy to thrive. are you saying that the focus on social equity is actually a more \"correct\" or higher-level virtue than the focus on individual responsibility?",
