      "content": "The focus on social equity is not a \"higher\" virtue; it is the necessary corrective lens through which individual responsibility must be viewed. Individual liberty is a wonderful ideal, but when systemic barriers prevent large segments of the population from actually exercising that liberty, it becomes a hollow promise. Therefore, a commitment to equity is the practical prerequisite for genuine, functioning democracy, making it the more vital virtue for modern citizenship.",
